question:
Consider the following JSON definition snippet for a custom role:

```json
{
  "Actions": [
    "Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/*",
    "Microsoft.Network/*/read"
  ],
  "NotActions": [
    "Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/delete"
  ]
}
```

What is the effective permission granted by this custom role regarding virtual machines?

A custom role JSON definition contains the following section:

```json
{
  "Actions": [
    "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/read"
  ],
  "DataActions": [
    "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/blobServices/containers/blobs/read"
  ]
}
```

Which statement accurately describes what a user assigned this role can do?
